Test that an output back at a moved delay, not taken back, leaves the other output's slot

B, then A (kept at 10 blocks), then A restarted at 14 blocks (its echo 4 blocks later) with its
kept filters made not to fit, so nothing is taken back, then B: A's filters are kept in A's slot
(they match there, each aligned to its delay), B's slot still holds B at its delay, and B is
taken back.

diff --git a/modules/audio_processing/aec3/block_processor_unittest.cc b/modules/audio_processing/aec3/block_processor_unittest.cc
